## Purpose
- Capture DB ownership and migration workflow for auth and organization services.

## Source of truth
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Data/AuthDbContext.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/Migrations/*.cs`
- `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth/appsettings*.json`
- `docker-compose.yml` / `docker-compose.staging.yml` (staging stack)
- `infrastructure/postgres/docker-compose.postgres.yml`
- `infrastructure/postgres/init/01-create-dbs-prod.sql`
- `aspire/TeamHub.AppHost/Program.cs` (local Aspire databases)

## Organization database

### Purpose
- Store organization/team/invitation data for `team-hub-organization`.

### Source of truth
- `services/team-hub-organization/team-hub-organization/Data/OrganizationDbContext.cs`
- `services/team-hub-organization/team-hub-organization/Migrations/*`
- `services/team-hub-organization/.env.example` (optional local `dotnet run` only)
- `.env.staging.example` (staging Compose)

### Connection strings
- Aspire: injected by AppHost (`organization_db`)
- staging Compose (`ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production`): `Host=db-postgres;Port=5432;Database=organizationdb;Username=${POSTGRES_USER};Password=${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}`

### DB startup
- Aspire AppHost creates `auth_db` / `organization_db` / `notification_db`; EF `Database.Migrate()` applies schema on service start.
- `./scripts/compose-staging.sh up --build` — Postgres init script creates `authdb` / `organizationdb` / `notificationdb`; EF migrate in containers.
- Activity feed table: `organization_activities` (append-only audit/activity log per org; indexes on `(OrganizationId, OccurredAt)` and `(OrganizationId, Type, OccurredAt)`).
- Import/export jobs table: `import_export_jobs` (async CSV/JSON import and export history per org; blob paths for source/result/errors).

## Organization API

See `docs/organization.mb` for `/api/organizations` contract.

## Do
- Use PostgreSQL for auth data only (users).
- Use Redis for refresh-token sessions (`auth:session:*`); Redis is shared infrastructure (`infrastructure/redis/`).
- Treat `AuthDbContext` as schema contract (`users`, indexes).
- Create schema changes through EF Core migrations in `Migrations/`.
- Keep connection string environment-aware:
  - Aspire: `auth_db` (injected)
  - staging auth container: `Host=db-postgres;Port=5432;Database=authdb;Username=${POSTGRES_USER};Password=${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}`
- Run local databases via Aspire AppHost (not Compose).
- Run staging database via `./scripts/compose-staging.sh` (`db-postgres-staging`, volume `postgres_data_staging`); init script creates `authdb` / `organizationdb` / `notificationdb`.

## Don't
- Do not edit migration history manually unless fixing broken migration state.
- Do not use direct SQL schema changes outside migrations.
- Do not assume postgres on host port `5432` for this project setup.
- Do not expect `docker-compose.dev.yml` to start Postgres (monitoring only).

## Checklist
- New/changed model has migration and snapshot update.
- DB startup path works with Aspire and staging Compose postgres.
- Unique constraints (username) remain intentional.
